CAT = "sgm5Notices"; SEG = "NOT"
Q = [
('Which MAS notice sets the balanced scorecard framework for representatives and supervisors?',
 'FAA-N20', ['FAA-N16', 'FAA-N06', 'FAA-N26'],
 'FAA-N20 sets the balanced scorecard framework and the independent sales audit unit. FAA-N16 covers recommendations, FAA-N06 AML/CFT and FAA-N26 competency.'),
("The balanced scorecard links part of a representative's variable income to:",
 'Non-sales KPIs', ['Number of new clients only', 'Total premiums sold', 'Length of service'],
 'Under FAA-N20, specified variable income is measured against non-sales KPIs on the quality of advice, so selling more cannot make up for poor advice.'),
('Which is one of the four non-sales KPIs in FAA-N20?',
 'Suitability of advice', ['Speed of closing sales', 'Number of referrals', 'Size of the client base'],
 "The four non-sales KPIs are understanding the client's needs, suitability of product recommendations, adequacy of information disclosure, and standards of professionalism and ethical conduct."),
("A representative influences a client's answers on the fact-find form. Which non-sales KPI is most directly breached?",
 'Understanding client needs', ['Adequacy of disclosure', 'Professionalism only', 'None, if the sale suits'],
 "KPI 1 looks at whether all pertinent information was collected and documented, whether the fact-find came before advice, and whether the representative influenced the client's inputs."),
('A representative paid only by variable income has what share of it measured against the non-sales KPIs?',
 '60%', ['40%', '75%', '100%'],
 'FAA-N20 measures 60% of variable income where a representative earns variable income only, and all of the variable income where he has a fixed salary plus variable pay.'),
('A representative earns a fixed salary plus variable income. How much of the variable income is measured?',
 'All of it', ['60% of it', 'Half of it', 'None of it'],
 'Where remuneration combines a fixed salary and variable income, FAA-N20 measures all of the variable income against the non-sales KPIs.'),
('Who carries out post-transaction checks under the balanced scorecard framework?',
 'The ISA unit', ["The representative's supervisor", 'The product issuer', "The client's bank"],
 'FAA-N20 requires an independent sales audit (ISA) unit, independent of the advisory business, to check sampled transactions. A compliance or risk function, or a third party, may take on the role.'),
("The ISA unit's post-transaction checks on a sampled transaction include a documentation review and:",
 'A client survey', ['A home visit', 'A credit check', 'A product rating'],
 'For most sampled transactions, FAA-N20 requires the ISA unit to review the FAA-N16 documentation and survey the client.'),
('Under FAA-N20, a Category 1 infraction includes recommending a product that is:',
 'Clearly unsuitable', ['Sent with late paperwork', 'From a newly licensed insurer', 'Paid for by GIRO'],
 "Category 1 infractions have a material impact on the client's interests or impinge on fitness and propriety, such as clearly unsuitable advice, needless switching or misrepresentation."),
('A representative forgets to write the names of dependants on a fact-find, and it does not affect the needs analysis. Under FAA-N20 it:',
 'May be disregarded', ['Is a Category 1 infraction', 'Leads straight to grade E', 'Must be reported to the police'],
 "FAA-N20 lets the ISA unit disregard minor lapses or administrative oversights that do not affect the client's interest or fitness and propriety, though prevalent lapses must be assessed."),
('Under FAA-N20, any case with a Category 1 infraction puts the representative in grade:',
 'E', ['B', 'C', 'D'],
 'Grade E applies where 30% or more of cases have infractions, five or more cases have Category 2 infractions, or one or more cases have a Category 1 infraction.'),
('A grade A representative is entitled to what share of specified variable income for the quarter?',
 '100%', ['75%', '50%', '80%'],
 'Grade A, with fewer than 5% of cases with infractions or one case with Category 2 infractions, keeps all specified variable income.'),
('A selected representative is one graded B or worse for how many consecutive quarters?',
 'Two', ['One', 'Three', 'Four'],
 'FAA-N20 defines a selected representative as one with grade B or worse in the two calendar quarters immediately before the measurement quarter.'),
("For a representative who is not a selected representative, the ISA unit's first round samples at least:",
 '5% of transactions', ['1% of transactions', '10% of transactions', '50% of transactions'],
 "FAA-N20's first round samples at least 5% of the population for most representatives and at least 10% for selected representatives, with further rounds if infractions turn up."),
("Besides sampled transactions, which finding feeds into a representative's balanced scorecard?",
 'A substantiated complaint', ['An unproven rumour', "A client's late payment", "A competitor's criticism"],
 'FAA-N20 counts infractions from sampled transactions, mystery shopping findings and substantiated complaints.'),
('A financial adviser adds its own sales targets to its scorecard. Under FAA-N20 it may NOT:',
 'Measure specified income on them', ['Include other KPIs at all', 'Reward good service', 'Keep scorecard records'],
 'An adviser may add other KPIs for its business, but specified variable income must be measured only against the non-sales KPIs.'),
('Supervisors are also covered by the balanced scorecard. Their specified variable income depends on:',
 "Their representatives' grades", ["The firm's share price", 'Their own sales volume only', 'Client entertainment budgets'],
 "FAA-N20 measures a supervisor's specified variable income against the performance of the representatives under his supervision."),
('Under FAA-N20, a rider bought together with a life policy is counted as:',
 'Part of one transaction', ['A separate transaction', 'Not a transaction at all', 'Two transactions'],
 'FAA-N20 says a rider purchased with a life policy is not counted as a separate transaction for post-transaction checks.'),
('FAA-N20 requires a financial adviser to give representatives a way to:',
 'Appeal their grade', ['Choose their own grade', 'Skip the ISA checks', 'Sample their own cases'],
 'FAA-N20 requires a process for representatives and supervisors to appeal, including on their grade or the infractions found.'),
('To advise on and arrange life policies, a representative needs RES5 and which product module?',
 'M9', ['M8', 'CM-EIP', 'M6A'],
 'FAA-N26 pairs RES5 with M9 for life policies that are Excluded Investment Products, and M9A as well for investment-linked policies that are Specified Investment Products.'),
("To advise on units in collective investment schemes, a representative's product module is:",
 'M8', ['M9', 'HI', 'BCP'],
 'Under FAA-N26, collective investment schemes need M8, plus M8A for those that are Specified Investment Products, or the combined CM-CIS.'),
('An individual who passed the old CMFAS Module 5 under the cancelled notice is treated as having passed:',
 'RES5', ['M9A', 'CM-SIP', 'None of the current modules'],
 "FAA-N26 replaced FAA-N13 on 1 April 2024 and deems a valid Module 5 pass, or SCI's non-examinable Module 5 course, to be a pass in RES5."),
('The first time a representative recommends an overseas-listed investment product to a client, he must give:',
 'A risk warning statement', ['A welcome gift voucher', 'A tax residency certificate', 'A performance guarantee'],
 "FAA-N16 requires the risk warning statement in its Annex 4, and the client's acknowledgement, before the first recommendation on an Overseas-Listed Investment Product."),
('Communications with a client about a Listed Specified Investment Product must be kept as:',
 'File notes or recordings', ['Memory only', 'Social media posts', 'Notes destroyed after the trade'],
 'FAA-N16 requires records of all communication on advice for listed SIPs, including a file note or tape recording of phone conversations.'),
]
